<title>USA: FP&amp;L St Lucie 1 nuke unit restarting Wed.</title>
<headline>FP&amp;L St Lucie 1 nuke unit restarting Wed.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Florida Power and Light Co's (FP&amp;L) 839 megawatt (MW) St Lucie 1 nuclear power unit was expected to restart Wednesday, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission said in its daily plant status report.</p>
<p>The unit tripped off line Tuesday due to a vibration in a reactor coolant pump.  </p>
<p>The company was not immediately available to confirm the restart.</p>
<p>The adjacent unit 2, with an identical generating capacity, was operating at full power.</p>
<p>Both units are located in Hutchinson Island, Fla.</p>
<p>FP&amp;L is a unit of FPL Group Inc.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
